      "body": "## Motivation\n\nI have three SM120 and MoE PRs open here, and every CI round so far has waited on someone to apply `run-ci`. #47248 is covered by the per-commit CPU unit suite, so `/run-cpu-ci` would verify it on hosted runners without taking a GPU runner. Asking for that cheap path.\n\n## Modifications\n\nAdd `xulunfan` to `.github/CI_PERMISSIONS.json` with label and rerun permissions, cooldown `0` (what `/run-cpu-ci` gates on), and reason `MoE and SM120 PRs`. The reason is not `top contributor`, so `update_ci_permission.py` keeps the entry on its next run. If a zero cooldown is more than you want to grant, label and rerun permissions with a small cooldown still help me — that just means full `run-ci` rounds instead of CPU-only ones.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #40862824181](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40862824181)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40862824268](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40862824268)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
